---
import CaseStudyPage from '@components/site/case-study/CaseStudyPage.astro';
import CaseStudyStats from '@components/site/case-study/CaseStudyStats.astro';
import PullQuote from '@components/site/case-study/PullQuote.astro';
import { customerStories } from '@lib/customer-stories';

// Every quote and figure on this page is verbatim from Mautic's own post
// (SOURCE_URL). Paraphrase only the narrative around them, and don't add
// figures the post doesn't state.
const SOURCE_URL = 'https://mautic.org/blog/keep-docs-up-to-date-automatically/';
const AUTHOR = 'Ayu Adiati';
const AUTHOR_ROLE = 'Mautic';

const story = customerStories.find((s) => s.slug === 'mautic')!;
---

<CaseStudyPage
  slug="mautic"
  title={story.title}
  description="Mautic's docs fell entire release versions behind. With Promptless drafting a docs PR for every code PR, 129 Promptless docs PRs merged in about four months, roughly 3.5 times faster than docs written by hand."
  company="Mautic"
  logo={story.logo}
  dek="Mautic is built by volunteers, and its docs had fallen entire release versions behind the code. Now Promptless drafts a docs PR for each code PR, and the developer and the Education Team review every one before it merges."
  facts={[
    { label: 'Company', value: 'Mautic, open-source marketing automation' },
    { label: 'Team', value: 'Volunteer developers and an EU-based Education Team' },
    { label: 'Docs', value: 'User and developer documentation, with a branch for each supported Mautic version' },
    { label: 'Workflow', value: 'A Promptless docs PR for each code PR on mautic/mautic' },
  ]}
  source={{ label: `Told by Mautic: read ${AUTHOR}'s post on the Mautic blog (Sep 3, 2026)`, href: SOURCE_URL }}
>
  <p>
    In September 2026, Mautic published a post on its own blog about how it keeps its docs up to date with Promptless.
    This page summarizes that post. The quotes and figures are Mautic's own.
  </p>

  <CaseStudyStats
    stats={[
      {
        value: '129',
        label: 'Promptless docs PRs merged in about four months',
        detail: 'Over more than four years, 392 PRs from human contributors were merged.',
      },
      {
        value: '27 days',
        label: 'Average time from code merge to docs merge for Promptless updates',
        detail: 'Docs written by hand averaged 98 days.',
      },
      {
        value: '~3.5×',
        label: 'Faster docs turnaround',
        detail: '“That’s roughly 3.5 times faster.”',
      },
    ]}
    caption="Figures from Mautic's post. Turnaround times come from a sample of merged PRs."
  />

  <p class="pl-cs-kicker">The challenge</p>
  <h2>Docs fell behind by entire release versions</h2>
  <p>
    Developers who open pull requests on <a href="https://github.com/mautic/mautic">mautic/mautic</a> are volunteers who
    also juggle day jobs and other feature work. A docs update is important, but it rarely felt urgent.
  </p>

  <PullQuote
    quote="Writing docs updates is important, but it rarely felt urgent, so it kept getting pushed aside. It wasn’t anyone’s fault. It’s just what happens when docs depend on people who are already stretched thin."
    name={AUTHOR}
    role={AUTHOR_ROLE}
  />

  <p>
    Mautic's <a href="https://docs.mautic.org/">user documentation</a> and{' '}
    <a href="https://developer.mautic.org/">developer documentation</a> fell behind “not by days, but by entire release
    versions.” Users ran into outdated instructions or asked questions the code could already answer. And there was
    more than one branch to keep current: each docs repository has one per supported Mautic version.
  </p>

  <p class="pl-cs-kicker">The workflow</p>
  <h2>A docs PR for every code PR</h2>
  <p>
    Mautic found Promptless through the <a href="https://writetechhub.org/">WriteTech Hub</a> community and connected it
    to both docs repositories, across every active version branch.
  </p>

  <ol class="pl-cs-steps not-content">
    <li>
      <span><strong>A developer opens a PR on mautic/mautic.</strong> Promptless writes a docs update for the change. While
      the code PR is unmerged, the docs PR stays a draft.</span>
    </li>
    <li>
      <span><strong>The code PR merges.</strong> Promptless marks the docs PR ready for review.</span>
    </li>
    <li>
      <span><strong>The code changes in review.</strong> When the developer adds more changes, Promptless updates the docs
      draft to match.</span>
    </li>
    <li>
      <span><strong>People review it.</strong> The developer confirms the draft matches what they built, and the Education
      Team reviews grammar, wording, and style as it would any docs contribution.</span>
    </li>
  </ol>

  <p>
    Mautic didn't start with full automation. At first, Promptless posted suggestions on its dashboard, and the Education
    Team reviewed each one before turning it into a PR. Once the team saw how consistently Promptless followed its style
    guide and the intent of each code change, it opted into the fully automated workflow.
  </p>

  <PullQuote
    quote="That trial period built trust in the tool before we handed over more of the process."
    name={AUTHOR}
    role={AUTHOR_ROLE}
  />

  <p class="pl-cs-kicker">The results</p>
  <h2>Docs that keep up with releases</h2>
  <p>“Since Promptless joined, the numbers tell a clear story,” Mautic writes. Turnaround time backs it up:</p>

  <figure class="pl-cs-compare not-content">
    <p class="pl-cs-compare-title">Average days from code merge to docs merge</p>
    <div class="pl-cs-compare-row pl-cs-compare-row-highlight">
      <span class="pl-cs-compare-label">Drafted by Promptless</span>
      <span class="pl-cs-compare-track">
        <span class="pl-cs-compare-bar" style="--pl-cs-bar: calc((100% - 4.5rem) * 27 / 98)"></span>
        <span class="pl-cs-compare-value">27 days</span>
      </span>
    </div>
    <div class="pl-cs-compare-row">
      <span class="pl-cs-compare-label">Written by hand</span>
      <span class="pl-cs-compare-track">
        <span class="pl-cs-compare-bar" style="--pl-cs-bar: calc(100% - 4.5rem)"></span>
        <span class="pl-cs-compare-value">98 days</span>
      </span>
    </div>
    <figcaption>From a sample of merged PRs, as reported in Mautic's post.</figcaption>
  </figure>

  <p>The clearest sign of progress, according to Mautic, is the release gap itself:</p>

  <CaseStudyStats
    stats={[
      { value: '7.0', label: 'The app had moved to 7.0', detail: 'while the docs were stuck at 5.2, two versions behind.' },
      { value: '7.1', label: 'Docs started catching up' },
      { value: '7.2', label: 'Docs were moving fast', detail: 'right when the automated Promptless workflow began.' },
    ]}
  />

  <p class="pl-cs-kicker">Human review</p>
  <h2>A person still makes the final call</h2>
  <p>
    Every Promptless draft goes through the same review as any other contribution, and Mautic's post is candid about what
    that review catches:
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li>
      Promptless once drafted a new section for an updated dropdown menu, but the improved labels already made the feature
      self-explanatory. The code PR's author caught it, and Promptless withdrew the PR.
    </li>
    <li>
      Another draft described a button that no longer existed and a limit already removed from the code. The author
      flagged it, Promptless checked the codebase and fixed the draft, and the Education Team merged it.
    </li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    Those issues fade over time. Promptless has gotten progressively more accurate, “partly because we train it directly
    on what to remember, and partly because it picks up on patterns from our corrections.”
  </p>

  <PullQuote
    quote="Nothing beats a human check before docs go live, and that’s exactly how we use Promptless: a fast first draft, with a person making the final call."
    name={AUTHOR}
    role={AUTHOR_ROLE}
  />

  <p class="pl-cs-kicker">Working together</p>
  <h2>Promptless adapts to Mautic's workflow</h2>
  <p>
    Mautic's Education Team is in the EU, and the Promptless team works US hours. Even so, “most questions get an answer
    within hours, or by their next morning at the latest.” Fixes usually ship within days, sometimes a week, and several
    of the things Mautic ran into became improvements to the core product.
  </p>

  <PullQuote
    quote="When something doesn’t fit Mautic’s setup, they don’t ask us to change how we work. They jump on a call, dig in with us, and adjust Promptless to match our workflow instead."
    name={AUTHOR}
    role={AUTHOR_ROLE}
  />

  <PullQuote
    size="large"
    quote="Promptless helped us catch up without asking already-busy developers to do more."
    name={AUTHOR}
    role={AUTHOR_ROLE}
    href={SOURCE_URL}
  />

  <p>
    Read the whole story in Mautic's words:{' '}
    <a href={SOURCE_URL} data-track-action="read_customer_source" data-track-funnel="evaluation" data-track-location="case_study_body" data-track-campaign="mautic">How Mautic pairs Promptless with human review to catch up on docs</a>.
  </p>
</CaseStudyPage>
